    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6125\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to big\ngame hunting authorization for the county of Onondaga; and providing for\nthe repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow the hunting of big game through the\nuse of a rifle in Onondaga County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend Paragraph a of subdivision 2 of\nsection 11-0907 of the Environmental Conservation Law by adding a new\nitem (o) to allow rifle hunting of big game in Onondaga County from the\nfirst Saturday after November 15 through the first Sunday after December\n7.\n\nSection 2 of this bill would amend Item (f) of paragraph a of subdivi-\nsion 2 of section 11-0907 of the Environmental Conservation Law to\ninclude a new item (o) to allow rifle hunting of big game in Onondaga\nCounty from the first Monday after November 15 through the first Tuesday\nafter December 7.\n\nSection 3 of this bill would amend Paragraph a of subdivision 2 of\nsection 11-0907 of the Environmental Conservation Law by adding a new\nitem (m) to allow rifle hunting of big game in Onondaga County from the\nfirst Saturday after November 15 through the first Sunday after December\n7.\n\nSection 4 of this bill would amend Item (f) of paragraph a of subdivi-\nsion 2 of section 11-0907 of the Environmental Conservation Law to\ninclude a new item (m) to allow rifle hunting of big game in Onondaga\nCounty from the first Monday after November 15 through the first Tuesday\nafter December 7.\n\nSection 5 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBig game hunting, which includes the hunting of deer and bear, is a\npopular sport enjoyed by over 700,000 State residents each year.\nCurrently, hunters across the State are permitted to use certain types\nof firearms to hunt big game. However, two upstate counties are not\nauthorized to hunt big game with rifles - Onondaga and Livingston Coun-\nties.\n\nHunting is a sport thousands of State residents enjoy every year, it is\nalso a crucial conservation tool that keeps deer and bear populations in\ncheck. Due to a variety of factors, the State's deer population has\nrapidly increased to over 1.2 million. Deer overabundance can negatively\nimpact farmers, homeowners, and foresters, while also causing road\nhazards across the State.  According to the Department of Environmental\n\nConservation hunters take around 220,000 deer annually, reducing the\nproblems that accompany deer overabundance.\n\nSince 2005, several counties in the Finger Lakes Region, Central New\nYork, and the Southern Tier have permitted hunting big game with rifles\nwith very few reported incidents or problems. Most recently, in 2020,\nTompkins County was authorized for the use of rifles in hunting big\ngame. In that timespan, there have been no serious incidents reported.\nThis bill would authorize big game hunting with rifles in Onondaga Coun-\nty.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
